# SDD scratch workspace (ledger, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/

# The architecture boundary test writes REAL source files into src/ and deletes
# them again. An interrupted run (Ctrl-C, CI timeout, OOM) leaves a node:fs or
# render import sitting in the one tree that must stay browser-loadable, which
# then makes `npm run depcruise` fail for a reason that has nothing to do with
# your change -- and a concurrent depcruise can see one mid-run even when the
# run is not interrupted (Task 4 reproduced exactly that flake).
#
# The glob, rather than a list: 2026-09-13's final review found this entry
# covered one of the four paths that test actually writes, the other three
# having been added later without it. `__name__.ts` is this repo's probe
# convention and nothing else uses it. Which files the test writes is not
# restated here -- `tests/architecture/boundary.test.ts` asserts that every one
# of them is ignored, so a fifth probe added without a matching rule fails the
# suite instead of rotting this comment.
src/**/__*__.ts

# Harness-managed worktrees
.claude/worktrees/
